fcpi patch 0010: enhanced route, browser extras and the principal's owner tag (FIRECRAWL_PI_SPEC.md §11, §12, §21.3)
Upstream 7666c1f9, after 0001-0009. The pi-resilient adapter accepts the enhanced proxy option and sends it as the
acquisition's route; registers the screenshot and actions features, sends them to the retrieval service held to the
safe subset, and returns each capture as a data URL for the gateway to store as an artifact; refuses any result that
carries target status 401, 403 or 429, so upstream's AddFeatureError retry cannot start outside the page's budget; and
reports the enhanced strategy as proxyUsed stealth. runWebScraper carries the gateway's owner tag from the job's origin
into internalOptions.fcpiOwner, which the adapter sends as the acquisition's principal and the PDF engine as the
parse request's owner (M5 review S1).

